{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "strain_divu_corner1",
    "description": "Scalar atom of the B-grid strain-rate divergence at corner 1 (the NE corner, the U point U(i,j)) of T cell (i,j): divu_1 = cyp*u(i,j) - dyT*u(i-1,j) + cxp*v(i,j) - dxT*v(i,j-1) (strain_rates, ice_dyn_shared.F90:2148-2151; the area-weighted form of divu = D(u,x) + D(v,y) on the B grid). The four U-point coordinates enter through the index params: oi/oj are the cell's own corner indices (oi = i, oj = j) and wim1/wjm1 are the west/south neighbor indices (i-1, j-1); the strain_rates_divu rule binds wim1 := 1 / wjm1 := 1 on the i = 1 / j = 1 halo strips, reproducing the Fortran's halo-copy of the velocity at the domain edge. The metric coefficients cxp/cyp/cxm/cym and cell dimensions dxT/dyT are scalars of the cell (ice_dyn_shared.F90:410-413, 433-437), bound by the rule to the cell's own values. Pure combination algebra: no faq, no index sets of its own.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:stencil", "family:cice_bgrid", "grid:cice_bgrid", "op:strain-rate"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hunke, E. C., et al. (2023). CICE v6.3.22 documentation and user's guide (LA-UR-23-31851), section on the EVP dynamics strain_rates."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "strain_divu_corner1": {
      "params": ["uvel", "vvel", "oi", "oj", "wim1", "wjm1", "cxp", "cyp", "cxm", "cym", "dxT", "dyT"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              { "op": "*", "args": ["cyp", { "op": "index", "args": ["uvel", "oi", "oj"] }] },
              { "op": "*", "args": ["dyT", { "op": "index", "args": ["uvel", "wim1", "oj"] }] }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              { "op": "*", "args": ["cxp", { "op": "index", "args": ["vvel", "oi", "oj"] }] },
              { "op": "*", "args": ["dxT", { "op": "index", "args": ["vvel", "oi", "wjm1"] }] }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
